window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>“I would burn the world to get to you if I could, but this is real life. And real life is not always the fairytale we want it to be.”<br> <br> Kristine Aguya<br> <br> With an upcoming challenge and the thought of Nolan’s death on the line, Emelia can’t seem to catch a break. Her entire world was thrown on its axis when Nolan walked into her life, and now she’s just supposed to let him sacrifice himself in some werewolf pissing contest? To make matters worse, although Mia had been returned to them, she seemed to be in some sort of magical coma. She was really getting sick of all these curveballs …<br> <br> Kristine Aguya was many things, but she prided herself most on being a good friend. With her basically vacant parents, her friends were everything to her. She didn’t have time to care about anything or anyone else, and frankly none of them were worth her time anyway. That was until a certain white wolf decided he refused to leave her alone. How annoying …<br> <br> With new enemies, unexpected visitor’s, and powers they still don’t understand will The Sacred burn hotter than ever, or go out like a match?</p>"; 
